State Management Hooks 
useState → Manages state in functional components. Returns a state variable and a function to update it.

2. Side Effect & Lifecycle Hooks
useEffect → Runs side effects (e.g., API calls, event listeners) after render. Can run on mount, update, or unmount.

useLayoutEffect → Similar to useEffect, but runs synchronously before browser painting, useful for layout adjustments.

3. Performance Optimization Hooks
useMemo → Memoizes values to avoid unnecessary recalculations during re-renders.
useCallback → Memoizes functions to prevent unnecessary re-creations function in child components.

4. Context & Ref Hooks
useContext → Provides a way to access context values without prop drilling.
useRef → Creates a mutable reference that persists across renders, often used for DOM manipulation.
useImperativeHandle → Customizes the ref object when using forwardRef, allowing parent components to control child components' functions.

5. Reducer Hook
useReducer → Alternative to useState for complex state logic, useful when state transitions depend on previous state values.

6. Custom Hooks
Custom Hooks → Created using built-in hooks to encapsulate and reuse logic across multiple components.
